A||||8||GT Bastard||Pics and results of head & manifold work...||||14||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||06-08-2000||04:36 PM||||Ok, here's my only decent pic of my ported and milled heads, and ported exhaust manifolds.  Everything is back together and running now, of course.  I will say this: I don't care what people think of my ass-o-meter, but this car pulls harder than it did before.  If I wasn't sure that it made a difference, I wouldn't have said anything at all.  The heads were sandblasted, milled .020, ported with a die grinder(by my father who HAS done this many times), and the valves seals were replaced(no more smoke on startup.)  I also had him port the exhaust manifolds to remove the restrictions.  I highly recommend this type of upgrade.  I had a blast ripping my motor apart and was pleased to find it clean as a whistle.  The car went from "Mr. Joe Blow 2.8"  to a very strong running motor.  Off the line it seems slightly better, but once it starts building up speed she pulls hard.  All in all, a very worth-while mod.  Sorry I don't have better pics of the porting... The close-ups came out fuzzy.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Heads.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Track.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||06-08-2000||05:18 PM||||Sweet. Looks like you were at a test n tune session, any track times with the new head work (and what did you run before)?  Did you lower the whole motor for the work, or just take it off the top?  Just curious.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||06-08-2000||06:17 PM||||We got rained out at the track on that day...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> No times yet.  I just removed the top end.  Didn't lower the cradle or anything. I plan on trying out the track again in the future, but I work on weekends.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wannabe||06-08-2000||09:37 PM||||In all of the web sites and discussions about the Fiero, I've only seen one that listed  mods and an et. It was an '87 GT with 5 speed, ported exhaust, flowmaster, no cat, K&N and 1.6 roller tip rocker arms. His et was 14.9x @93.xx mph (I don't remember the exact numbers)  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||06-09-2000||12:28 AM||||I'm really curious what it would run... Everyone tells me that 20hp would be a good estimate, but who knows?  Anyhow, hitting the track was a blast.  I'm going to start going there more often since it's only about a 30 minute drive.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mattsfiero||06-09-2000||04:43 AM||||The car looks sweet Man. Good luck on the track with it and thanks for the upgrade Idea. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Matt||||reg||10
Z||000006||Standard||06-09-2000||04:48 AM||||I'm seriously thinking about doing this... and it would give me a reason to start riding my bike into work... ||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||06-09-2000||07:04 AM||||I have said time after time that pocket porting will improve flow, which ultimately improves upper rpm power. Without a higher lift cam and headers to make full use of that new flow potential, I doubt you'll see a 20 HP gain, I'm guessing (with the help of my Desktop Dyno) it'll be more like a 10 pony gain for the porting and maybe up to a 5 HP increase with the ported manifolds. Now you need a new cam. Either the Crane CompuCam or the GM hipo one. Trouble is, they're hard to replace with the engine still in the car.||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||06-09-2000||04:33 PM||||I was actually thinking the same thing Batboy... I had considered dropping the motor and throwing in a cam.  Also, at the same time I was thinking of upgrading the fuel system.  With the new cam, I should be able to benefit from a bit more fuel.  Possibly something modest like 3.1 injectors and an adjustable fuel pressure regulator.  Any other ideas?||||reg||1
